┌ Warning: `energy_source_tags` tag `new_strat` lists `precipitation`, which cannot contribute to a source tag. It is the sedimentation of precipitating species, which moves energy between levels rather than adding it. Where water sediments, the tags follow it as transport instead, so nothing is credited to `precipitation`. The `energy_tracers` family does attribute it. Under 0-moment microphysics, rain leaves through `microphysics` instead. Note `moist` and `all` both expand to include `precipitation`.
